hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"772","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Salamah ibn Sakhr al-Ansari, he said: I was a man who had been given of desire for women what no one else had been given. When Ramadan came, I made zihar from my wife until it ended, fearing that I would approach her at night and then continue, until morning overtook me while I was unable to stop. While she was serving me one night, something of her was uncovered to me, so I fell upon her. In the morning I went to my people and told them my story, and said to them: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him of my matter. They said: No, by Allah, we will not do it; we fear that Quran will be revealed concerning us, or that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will say something about us whose disgrace will remain upon us. Rather, go and do as you see fit. So I went until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him my story. He said to me: Are you the one? I said: I am the one. He said: Are you the one? I said: I am the one. He said: Are you the one? I said: I am the one, so carry out the ruling of Allah concerning me, for I am patient and hopeful of reward. He said: Free a slave. He said: So I struck the side of my neck and said: By the One who sent you with the truth, O Messenger of Allah, I own nothing besides it this morning. He said: Then fast two consecutive months. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did what befell me befall me except because of fasting? He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, we spent our night destitute with no supper. He said: Go to the keeper of the charity of Banu Zurayq, and tell him to hand it over to you; feed on your behalf from it a wasq of dates to sixty poor persons, then seek help with the rest for yourself and your family. He said: So I returned to my people and said: I found with you hardship and bad counsel, and I found with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ease and blessing; he has ordered for me your charity, so hand it over to me. He said: So they handed it over to me."
"773","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Ibn Lahiah and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a man of Banu Zurayq called Salamah ibn Sakhr: then he mentioned the hadith similarly in abridged form, and said at its end: He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates, and he gave them to me, close to fifteen sa, and said: Give this in charity. He said: O Messenger of Allah, upon one poorer than me and my family? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat it, you and your family."
"774","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Mamar ibn Abdillah ibn Hanzalah, from Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn Salam, he said: Khuwaylah bint Thalabah narrated to me - and she was with Aws ibn Samit, the brother of Ubadah ibn al-Samit - she said: He came to me one day and spoke to me about something while annoyed, so I answered him back, and he became angry and said: You are to me as the back of my mother. Then he went out and sat in the gathering place of his people, then he returned and wanted me, so I refused him, and he wrestled me and I wrestled him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. So I said: No, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you shall not reach her until Allah judges concerning me and you. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of what I met from him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is your husband and your cousin, so fear Allah and keep good company with him. She said: I had not left before the Quran came down: Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband, until it reached the expiation. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Command him to free a slave. I said: By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, he has no slave to free. He said: Command him to fast two consecutive months. I said: O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man with no ability to fast. He said: Then let him feed sixty poor persons. I said: O Prophet of Allah, he has nothing with which to feed. He said: We shall help him with a basket of dates - and the basket is a container holding thirty sa. I said: And I shall help him with another basket. He said: You have done well; let him give it in charity."
"775","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Ammar narrated to me, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after having made zihar from his wife and then having intercourse with her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I made zihar from my wife and then I fell upon her before expiating. He said: What carried you to that, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I saw her anklet in the moonlight. He said: Do not approach her until you do what Allah the Exalted has commanded."
